      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:4:65:6",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) عَنْ رَجُلٍ اجْتَمَعَ عَلَيْهِ صَلَاةُ السَّنَةِ مِنْ مَرَضٍ قَالَ لَا يَقْضِي ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "A group, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Al Husayn Bin Saeed, from Safwan, from Al Ays Bin Al Qasim who said, ",
          "‘I asked Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> about a man upon whom the (lapse) Sunnah <span class=\"iTxt\">Salāt</span>s have been accumulated due to illness’. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘He would not (need to) fulfil’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "6. A group has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from al-Husayn ibn Sa‘id from Safwan from al-‘Is ibn al-Qasim who has said the following: “I once asked abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about a man upon whom Salah (prayer) for one year has accumulated because of illness. He (the Imam) said, ‘He is not required to perform such Salah (prayer).”’ "
        ]
      }
